  <processInformation>
    <dataSetInformation>
      <common:UUID>ada3283d-2a6f-4f30-93e0-039664b27d30</common:UUID>
      <name>
        <baseName xml:lang="en">Storage of chilled goods, cold storage, 1 week</baseName>
      </name>
      <common:synonyms>Stoccaggio in magazzino frigorifero di prodotti freschi per una settimana </common:synonyms>
      <classificationInformation>
        <common:classification name="ILCDCategories" classes="../ILCDClassification.xml">
          <common:class level="0">Systems</common:class>
          <common:class level="1">Other systems</common:class>
        </common:classification>
      </classificationInformation>
      <common:generalComment>The dataset has been developed in LIFE EFFIGE project. Details are given in “PEFCR of contracted supply service for school meals” (lifeeffige.eu). The background system is not included in the model. To complete the inventory, the use of data from other published database is necessary. The dataset includes the model of a Distribution Centre (DC). The DC space-time is allocated to chilled goods based on the DC capacity, the volume occupied by the product and the storage time. </common:generalComment>
    </dataSetInformation>
    <quantitativeReference type="Reference flow(s)">
      <referenceToReferenceFlow>0</referenceToReferenceFlow>
    </quantitativeReference>
    <time>
      <common:referenceYear>2018</common:referenceYear>
      <common:dataSetValidUntil>2024</common:dataSetValidUntil>
    </time>
    <geography>
      <locationOfOperationSupplyOrProduction location="IT"/>
    </geography>
    <technology>
      <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>The dataset includes the model of a Distribution Centre (DC) for dry, chilled and frozen storage.  The DC modelled is a 30000 m2 building, 10 m high, and with a 30,000 m2 parking. Life of the building is 80 years. Chilled and frozen storage areas are 30% of the total area. The area of services is 5% as well as the area of offices. The actual capacity of the DC has been assumed to be 72,000 m3 for ambient storage and 36,000 m3 for chilled/ frozen storage.  The model includes infrastructure and building; electricity, natural gas and water consumption; refrigerant gases consumption and leakages.  The DC impact per product has been calculated using an allocation based on the total storage capacity of the distribution centre.  The storage volume of chilled goods has been assumed to be three times their actual volume and chilled goods have been assumed to be stored for 1 week on average.  </technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
      <technologicalApplicability>Due to several assumptions and estimation included in the model, the dataset can be used for those cases where the impact of storage operations is not the main contribution to the total impact of the system. </technologicalApplicability>
    </technology>
  </processInformation>
